1
00:00:52,511 --> 00:00:53,345
ALL PERSONS, LOCATIONS, RELIGIONS,
INCIDENTS, AND ORGANIZATIONS IN THIS DRAMA

2
00:00:53,471 --> 00:00:54,305
ARE FICTITIOUS

3
00:00:54,430 --> 00:00:55,264
CHILD ACTORS HAVE FILMED SAFELY
UNDER PARENTAL SUPERVISION

4
00:00:55,389 --> 00:00:56,265
SCENES INVOLVING ANIMALS WERE FILMED
SAFELY WITH EXPERT ADVICE AND COOPERATION

5
00:00:58,100 --> 00:00:59,727
Let's get married, Mi-do.

6
00:01:04,607 --> 00:01:07,401
Marry me, Mi-do.

7
00:01:22,041 --> 00:01:27,922
3. CAN WE FEEL THAT SPARK AGAIN?

8
00:01:33,969 --> 00:01:35,638
It suddenly hit me.

9
00:01:37,264 --> 00:01:38,891
If I broke up with Namgung,

10
00:01:39,016 --> 00:01:41,811
how many chapters of my life
would disappear with him?

11
00:01:43,687 --> 00:01:47,191
Would I be okay
if I lost those parts of me?

12
00:01:54,907 --> 00:01:55,741
Or…

13
00:01:57,368 --> 00:02:00,287
Could I go on living without Namgung?

14
00:02:49,628 --> 00:02:50,838
His name is Namgung Ho.

15
00:02:52,923 --> 00:02:55,301
He's the same age as Mi-do…

16
00:02:55,426 --> 00:02:56,302
THE SORROWS OF YOUNG WERTHER

17
00:02:56,427 --> 00:02:59,054
…and he'll be living with us
starting today.

18
00:03:00,723 --> 00:03:03,183
Hoya, say hello to everyone.

19
00:03:05,269 --> 00:03:06,312
What's wrong?

20
00:03:06,437 --> 00:03:07,938
Are you feeling shy?

21
00:03:56,737 --> 00:03:58,113
Hot, hot, hot!

22
00:04:00,866 --> 00:04:03,744
-All right.
-What are you doing, sir?

23
00:04:03,869 --> 00:04:05,579
-Hey, come taste this.
-Pardon?

24
00:04:10,042 --> 00:04:11,001
It's hot.

25
00:04:14,588 --> 00:04:16,465
What is this? It tastes familiar.

26
00:04:18,175 --> 00:04:20,719
Corn Sticks, right?
The ones that were discontinued.

27
00:04:21,345 --> 00:04:22,596
Why are you making these?

28
00:04:22,721 --> 00:04:24,390
Okay.

29
00:04:27,059 --> 00:04:28,060
How's it going?

30
00:04:37,069 --> 00:04:38,529
Oh, seriously.

31
00:04:39,238 --> 00:04:41,323
Is Aunt Mi-do not coming this year either?

32
00:04:41,448 --> 00:04:44,618
It's her own dad's memorial.
Why does she always skip it?

33
00:04:46,704 --> 00:04:48,622
Can't you even wipe those dishes properly?

34
00:04:49,164 --> 00:04:50,874
They're still all wet, buddy.

35
00:04:52,668 --> 00:04:53,794
I  am  wiping.

36
00:05:26,827 --> 00:05:28,078
EXORCISM CHRONICLES

37
00:05:52,144 --> 00:05:53,687
Exorcism Chronicles  on a memorial?

38
00:05:55,731 --> 00:05:57,316
-Drink some water.
-Okay.

39
00:05:57,858 --> 00:06:00,360
So this is what Dad used to read.

40
00:06:01,403 --> 00:06:03,906
Dad always took me
to the bookstore in a stroller.

41
00:06:04,031 --> 00:06:05,783
There he goes, making things up again.

42
00:06:05,908 --> 00:06:08,494
I am not. I actually remember it.

43
00:06:08,619 --> 00:06:11,830
But I think he also read
a lot of comic books.

44
00:06:12,456 --> 00:06:13,957
Um, I have something to tell you--

45
00:06:14,083 --> 00:06:15,000
Nonsense.

46
00:06:15,584 --> 00:06:18,128
Dad only read novels.
Only fantasy martial arts ones.

47
00:06:18,253 --> 00:06:20,839
No, I remember it clearly.

48
00:06:20,964 --> 00:06:22,591
He looked really happy reading them.

49
00:06:22,716 --> 00:06:23,967
No, I'm telling you.

50
00:06:24,093 --> 00:06:28,972
He read  Mookhyang, Dragon Raja,
and  Temple of the Dragon.

51
00:06:29,098 --> 00:06:30,891
Strictly a fantasy martial arts guy.

52
00:06:31,016 --> 00:06:32,643
Right, Lee Mi-do? You remember.

53
00:06:32,768 --> 00:06:35,521
-We have something to say--
-No, I'm telling you.

54
00:06:35,646 --> 00:06:37,189
I do remember him reading comics

55
00:06:37,314 --> 00:06:38,607
and going to the bookstore.

56
00:06:38,732 --> 00:06:41,151
No, dude. You're just
making things up in your head.

57
00:06:41,276 --> 00:06:43,403
No, I'm right. Mom, isn't that right?

58
00:06:43,529 --> 00:06:44,988
Dad only read novels, right?

59
00:06:45,114 --> 00:06:46,240
We're getting married!

60
00:06:58,752 --> 00:07:03,423
But it's a bit embarrassing
when you all stare at me all of a sudden.

61
00:07:05,926 --> 00:07:06,844
Dad

62
00:07:07,761 --> 00:07:09,721
liked  Sunday Seoul.

63
00:07:16,478 --> 00:07:17,855
Do you guys remember?

64
00:07:19,231 --> 00:07:21,441
When I was about three and a half…

65
00:07:23,235 --> 00:07:25,612
a crazy dog lunged at Mi-do.

66
00:07:25,737 --> 00:07:26,989
Namgung.

67
00:07:27,114 --> 00:07:28,365
This is all your fault.

68
00:07:28,490 --> 00:07:30,993
You dropped him off a slide
when he was five.

69
00:07:31,118 --> 00:07:33,745
He's been undeniably weird ever since.

70
00:07:33,871 --> 00:07:35,747
I heard Mi-do scream,

71
00:07:35,873 --> 00:07:37,124
and you, Namgung,

72
00:07:38,250 --> 00:07:40,627
left me with Yeong-do
and ran straight to her.

73
00:07:40,752 --> 00:07:43,463
Man, I should've just let her get bitten.

74
00:07:43,589 --> 00:07:44,840
Come on.

75
00:07:47,593 --> 00:07:49,720
I'm joking. It's a joke.

76
00:07:51,138 --> 00:07:52,181
Anyway, that day…

77
00:07:53,015 --> 00:07:54,766
I remember that day so vividly.

78
00:07:54,892 --> 00:07:56,602
The wind,

79
00:07:57,352 --> 00:08:00,856
the temperature, the smell, and…

80
00:08:02,024 --> 00:08:03,400
Namgung's back

81
00:08:04,568 --> 00:08:05,819
as he ran to Mi-do.

82
00:08:08,280 --> 00:08:09,448
I knew right then.

83
00:08:11,575 --> 00:08:13,118
That you two would get married.

84
00:08:14,244 --> 00:08:17,039
Be honest. You heard that from Mom, right?

85
00:08:17,581 --> 00:08:18,999
So you've loved her since then?

86
00:08:19,124 --> 00:08:22,377
What? I was only ten.

87
00:08:23,170 --> 00:08:25,172
So you've loved her since you were ten?

88
00:08:25,714 --> 00:08:27,507
Oh, stop talking nonsense.

89
00:08:27,633 --> 00:08:29,259
Hey, let's just eat some  ramyeon.

90
00:08:35,891 --> 00:08:37,851
Didn't I nail the water ratio?

91
00:08:37,976 --> 00:08:40,729
I made the best  ramyeon
in my unit in the military.

92
00:08:51,323 --> 00:08:52,741
I'm not sure if I loved her,

93
00:08:53,867 --> 00:08:56,703
but I think I did want to protect her.

94
00:09:01,917 --> 00:09:03,543
From the moment I saw her,

95
00:09:04,253 --> 00:09:07,214
I thought, "She's just like me."

96
00:09:10,175 --> 00:09:11,176
I just knew.

97
00:09:13,470 --> 00:09:15,389
So you've loved her since you were seven?

98
00:09:16,890 --> 00:09:17,933
Just eat.

99
00:09:22,980 --> 00:09:23,855
Hello?

100
00:09:24,606 --> 00:09:26,108
What do you mean by that?

101
00:09:26,984 --> 00:09:30,237
Special lecture, my foot.
How many times is this now?

102
00:09:31,196 --> 00:09:33,156
I said to give me three days' notice.

103
00:09:33,282 --> 00:09:35,409
It's a last-minute special lecture.

104
00:09:35,534 --> 00:09:36,702
Think I want to go?

105
00:09:36,827 --> 00:09:39,121
You only see him once a month.

106
00:09:39,246 --> 00:09:40,747
Don't you feel bad for Sang-su?

107
00:09:40,872 --> 00:09:42,332
I do feel bad.

108
00:09:42,457 --> 00:09:45,210
That's why I called you, of all people.

109
00:09:45,335 --> 00:09:48,463
Why else would I be crazy enough
to call you like this?

110
00:09:49,381 --> 00:09:50,966
Oh, is that so?

111
00:09:51,091 --> 00:09:53,302
I'm so honored that it's pissing me off.

112
00:09:53,427 --> 00:09:54,303
Wow.

113
00:09:55,012 --> 00:09:57,389
Have you still not gotten over
your victim complex?

114
00:09:57,514 --> 00:10:00,183
Do yourself a favor
and fix that before you turn 50.

115
00:10:00,309 --> 00:10:02,019
What? Victim complex?

116
00:10:02,144 --> 00:10:02,978
Hey, you menace!

117
00:10:03,103 --> 00:10:05,147
What, you petty little jerk?

118
00:10:05,272 --> 00:10:08,233
Petty? What did you just call me?

119
00:10:08,358 --> 00:10:09,609
You're the selfish one…

120
00:10:09,735 --> 00:10:12,154
Good thing we didn't bring Sang-su, right?

121
00:10:12,279 --> 00:10:13,238
Seriously, don't.

122
00:10:13,363 --> 00:10:15,157
They wouldn't fight with him here.

123
00:10:15,282 --> 00:10:16,408
I'm fine.

124
00:10:16,533 --> 00:10:17,367
You think?

125
00:10:17,492 --> 00:10:19,411
Think of the kid.

126
00:10:19,536 --> 00:10:21,580
I came fishing,
and now you're telling me this?

127
00:10:23,707 --> 00:10:24,916
How deep are you fishing today?

128
00:10:25,042 --> 00:10:28,670
Forget it. Whatever.
I don't need it. I don't…

129
00:10:28,795 --> 00:10:30,630
Today, I'm fishing…

130
00:10:32,382 --> 00:10:34,343
-at 110m.
-Why send money? No need to.

131
00:10:34,468 --> 00:10:36,845
-That's pretty deep.
-We have enough already, don't we?

132
00:10:36,970 --> 00:10:39,348
Goodness. You're right.

133
00:10:39,473 --> 00:10:41,475
Nothing has changed since then.

134
00:10:47,272 --> 00:10:48,106
Mom.

135
00:10:48,231 --> 00:10:49,566
QUEENS HAIR SALON

136
00:10:49,691 --> 00:10:50,901
If…

137
00:10:51,693 --> 00:10:53,904
I were to die before Namgung…

138
00:10:56,865 --> 00:10:58,909
I'm being serious, so listen to me.

139
00:10:59,034 --> 00:11:02,579
Why are you jinxing yourself
before your wedding?

140
00:11:02,704 --> 00:11:04,831
-Knock on wood.
-Knock, knock. Happy?

141
00:11:05,582 --> 00:11:06,750
Hear me out first.

142
00:11:08,251 --> 00:11:10,921
You never know what will happen.

143
00:11:12,589 --> 00:11:15,008
You didn't know Dad
would die so early either.

144
00:11:16,093 --> 00:11:17,427
Anyway…

145
00:11:17,552 --> 00:11:20,722
If I die before Namgung does,

146
00:11:22,432 --> 00:11:25,227
give this building to him instead of me.

147
00:11:27,062 --> 00:11:29,231
If I die and you don't,

148
00:11:29,356 --> 00:11:30,190
I'll haunt you.

149
00:11:30,315 --> 00:11:31,733
Hey!

150
00:11:31,858 --> 00:11:33,318
Why are you yelling?

151
00:11:33,443 --> 00:11:36,154
Even if you're alive,
everything's going to Hoya anyway,

152
00:11:36,279 --> 00:11:38,740
so don't you worry about that.

153
00:11:39,449 --> 00:11:41,159
Don't count your chickens yet.

154
00:11:41,284 --> 00:11:44,204
No, that's not right.
Give it to me while I'm alive.

155
00:11:44,329 --> 00:11:46,873
He and I will share, so give it to me.

156
00:11:46,998 --> 00:11:50,043
Good grief,
what's the point of having three kids?

157
00:11:50,168 --> 00:11:52,921
The only one who looks out for me is Hoya.

158
00:11:54,673 --> 00:11:57,467
He replaces the window screens
when summer rolls around,

159
00:11:57,592 --> 00:12:01,763
and buys insulation covers in winter
so the pipes don't freeze.

160
00:12:01,888 --> 00:12:05,934
He regularly cleans the AC
and checks the boiler.

161
00:12:06,059 --> 00:12:08,687
Even when the paint on the rooftop
peeled off,

162
00:12:08,812 --> 00:12:10,772
Hoya was the one who repainted it.

163
00:12:10,897 --> 00:12:16,111
Last week, he even
put anti-slip strips on the stairs.

164
00:12:16,236 --> 00:12:17,737
Didn't he do that last year?

165
00:12:17,863 --> 00:12:19,823
I tell him it's fine,

166
00:12:19,948 --> 00:12:23,201
but he comes and replaces them
around this time every year.

167
00:12:24,703 --> 00:12:26,037
Maybe that's why.

168
00:12:26,163 --> 00:12:28,874
Whenever Hoya puts down
new anti-slip strips,

169
00:12:28,999 --> 00:12:31,543
it finally feels like winter has arrived.

170
00:12:35,547 --> 00:12:36,548
Well…

171
00:12:38,300 --> 00:12:40,135
Have you talked about that with Hoya?

172
00:12:41,094 --> 00:12:43,430
You're getting married.
You should at least reach out…

173
00:12:45,932 --> 00:12:47,934
Don't even think about
mentioning it to Namgung.

174
00:12:48,059 --> 00:12:51,062
Look at those daggers.

175
00:12:57,360 --> 00:12:58,945
To Namgung, his only family

176
00:13:00,113 --> 00:13:03,492
are me, you, Lee Yeong-do,

177
00:13:05,076 --> 00:13:07,787
our youngest, and Lee Sang-su.

178
00:13:09,247 --> 00:13:10,499
There's no one else.

179
00:13:13,376 --> 00:13:15,462
So if I die, Namgung gets this building--

180
00:13:17,631 --> 00:13:18,715
Jeez!

181
00:13:26,932 --> 00:13:29,059
What? When did you get here?

182
00:13:29,768 --> 00:13:30,727
Just now.

183
00:13:32,270 --> 00:13:34,022
You kept tossing and turning.

184
00:13:35,148 --> 00:13:37,317
I took a short nap earlier. That's why.

185
00:13:40,070 --> 00:13:40,946
Mi-do.

186
00:13:44,199 --> 00:13:46,117
Every year on your dad's memorial,

187
00:13:47,160 --> 00:13:50,455
I pretended not to notice
since you wanted to be alone.

188
00:13:50,580 --> 00:13:52,415
But be with us, starting this year.

189
00:13:55,168 --> 00:13:56,169
You don't want to?

190
00:13:58,463 --> 00:14:01,716
No, I want to do that too.

191
00:14:06,054 --> 00:14:06,888
Come.

192
00:14:21,403 --> 00:14:23,572
Shouldn't you see a doctor?

193
00:14:23,697 --> 00:14:26,366
I'll go if it lasts until this weekend.

194
00:14:27,117 --> 00:14:28,827
-Promise?
-Yes.

195
00:14:39,838 --> 00:14:40,755
Namgung.

196
00:14:43,425 --> 00:14:45,719
I want that spark back with you.

197
00:14:49,889 --> 00:14:53,435
And I hope you feel it with me, too.

198
00:15:43,777 --> 00:15:45,904
-Is that from work?
-It's fine. Just ignore it.

199
00:15:49,115 --> 00:15:51,159
It's bothering me. Just answer it.

200
00:15:51,284 --> 00:15:52,369
No, it's fine.

201
00:15:57,415 --> 00:15:58,541
Sorry, just a second.

202
00:16:07,801 --> 00:16:08,802
Yes, sir.

203
00:16:11,346 --> 00:16:14,099
I'll call them and get right back to you.

204
00:16:14,808 --> 00:16:15,684
Okay.

205
00:16:17,227 --> 00:16:18,228
Sorry.

206
00:16:23,233 --> 00:16:24,234
Hey, Sang-hun.

207
00:16:24,359 --> 00:16:25,777
La Vita's local factory

208
00:16:25,902 --> 00:16:28,947
recalled everything
due to aflatoxin levels.

209
00:16:29,072 --> 00:16:30,865
I'll call their headquarters,

210
00:16:30,990 --> 00:16:32,242
so check on things there.

211
00:16:33,243 --> 00:16:34,536
Yes, as soon as possible.

212
00:16:34,661 --> 00:16:36,538
HUNMIN CONFECTIONERY

213
00:16:37,747 --> 00:16:39,040
It won't be easy,

214
00:16:39,165 --> 00:16:42,252
but La Vita wants to meet,
so I'll report back after.

215
00:16:42,377 --> 00:16:44,003
Work your magic on them.

216
00:16:44,129 --> 00:16:45,004
Yes, sir.

217
00:16:56,933 --> 00:16:57,767
MIDORI

218
00:16:57,892 --> 00:16:59,102
Midori, asleep?

219
00:16:59,227 --> 00:17:00,562
Work stuff got sorted out.

220
00:17:00,687 --> 00:17:02,397
Texting so you don't worry.

221
00:17:07,277 --> 00:17:10,363
As soon as things settle down with work,
let's go on a trip.

222
00:17:10,488 --> 00:17:12,073
To Taipei, which you love.

223
00:17:12,198 --> 00:17:14,868
Although, warm Hawaii would be nice too.

224
00:17:21,249 --> 00:17:22,625
Huh? What?

225
00:17:23,585 --> 00:17:25,462
I thought you'd come after lunch.

226
00:17:27,297 --> 00:17:29,924
This is Park Su-a from Snack Team 4.

227
00:17:30,049 --> 00:17:32,343
She's been assigned to our team today.

228
00:17:32,469 --> 00:17:34,554
We'll be working together. Say hello.

229
00:17:35,096 --> 00:17:38,433
Hello. My name is Park Su-a.
I look forward to working with you.

230
00:17:44,773 --> 00:17:47,859
I feel like I made my stance
clear enough last time.

231
00:17:47,984 --> 00:17:50,570
You're clingier than I thought, Ms. Park.

232
00:17:54,824 --> 00:17:57,410
Jeong Yeon-ho and Seok Dong-hwan
of Purchasing,

233
00:17:57,535 --> 00:17:58,745
Yoon Jae-mun of Snack Team 4,

234
00:17:58,870 --> 00:18:00,288
Jeong Seok-ho of Distribution,

235
00:18:00,413 --> 00:18:01,581
and Baek Seok-u of Finance.

236
00:18:02,707 --> 00:18:06,461
Most of Executive Director Yoon's people
are involved.

237
00:18:11,633 --> 00:18:15,678
The reason TF Snack Team 3's
fourth sample tasted different

238
00:18:16,262 --> 00:18:18,181
is because they used
imported sweet potatoes.

239
00:18:20,225 --> 00:18:21,184
It was a mistake.

240
00:18:22,602 --> 00:18:26,356
So from now on, they'll be extra careful
when scheduling samples.

241
00:18:26,940 --> 00:18:30,401
The date they flat-out refuse to offer
during schedule coordination

242
00:18:30,527 --> 00:18:34,155
will be the day they make the switch.

243
00:18:35,198 --> 00:18:37,158
So you're approaching me like this

244
00:18:37,283 --> 00:18:39,828
to find out that exact date?

245
00:18:42,163 --> 00:18:44,999
Just let me tag along
when they schedule the sample.

246
00:18:46,376 --> 00:18:49,003
I know I'm being selfish,
but you can do that much.

247
00:18:49,587 --> 00:18:50,964
I'll handle the rest myself.

248
00:19:01,349 --> 00:19:03,268
Are you really not?

249
00:19:07,063 --> 00:19:10,191
The more I look, the more you resemble
Executive Director Yoon.

250
00:19:10,817 --> 00:19:12,652
Here. Wow!

251
00:19:12,777 --> 00:19:14,696
You look even more alike when you frown.

252
00:19:20,076 --> 00:19:21,119
Okay, got it.

253
00:19:21,786 --> 00:19:23,705
You're not related
to Executive Director Yoon.

254
00:19:24,831 --> 00:19:26,291
You're just prickly.

255
00:19:27,709 --> 00:19:30,086
Let's eat. There's less
than 30 minutes left for lunch.

256
00:19:31,713 --> 00:19:33,882
It won't interfere with Team 3's work.

257
00:19:34,632 --> 00:19:38,720
Let me tag along on the day we schedule
the samples with the factory manager.

258
00:19:39,929 --> 00:19:41,890
I don't think I can do that.

259
00:19:42,599 --> 00:19:46,144
If an inner-circle scandal breaks out,
the company will start an investigation,

260
00:19:46,269 --> 00:19:49,689
which means the new product project
using the crop will be put on hold.

261
00:19:49,814 --> 00:19:51,399
Unless I've lost my mind,

262
00:19:51,524 --> 00:19:53,651
I wouldn't back a move
that hurts our team.

263
00:19:54,569 --> 00:19:55,486
Just eat your noodles.

264
00:20:00,158 --> 00:20:01,242
But…

265
00:20:01,367 --> 00:20:04,287
If we launch it in this state,
the quality will be poor.

266
00:20:04,412 --> 00:20:06,664
We couldn't possibly get
good results in the market.

267
00:20:06,789 --> 00:20:07,999
You know that too.

268
00:20:13,630 --> 00:20:14,589
I do know.

269
00:20:15,590 --> 00:20:18,968
But you seem to be missing
what's really important.

270
00:20:20,720 --> 00:20:23,264
Our team won't be scheduling
any production for a while.

271
00:20:25,266 --> 00:20:28,686
The peperoncino supplier for the seasoning
is having some issues.

272
00:20:28,811 --> 00:20:29,646
What?

273
00:20:29,771 --> 00:20:33,775
And contrary to my looks,
I have an awful personality.

274
00:20:33,900 --> 00:20:35,568
I'm also a total boomer,

275
00:20:35,693 --> 00:20:38,071
so I get easily offended and triggered,

276
00:20:38,196 --> 00:20:39,697
and I throw lots of fits.

277
00:20:40,782 --> 00:20:45,161
The problem is that starting today,
I'm your direct supervisor.

278
00:20:45,745 --> 00:20:48,039
Do you grasp the situation now?

279
00:20:54,003 --> 00:20:58,091
Damn it. This is driving me crazy.

280
00:20:58,216 --> 00:21:00,093
JAEKANG LAW FIRM

281
00:21:30,707 --> 00:21:32,667
Remember what you said to me back then?

282
00:21:33,292 --> 00:21:35,378
I'd like to return the favor now.

283
00:21:35,503 --> 00:21:39,298
You will never make
your feature film debut.

284
00:21:40,717 --> 00:21:43,761
You've lost your drive
and become stagnant.

285
00:21:43,886 --> 00:21:46,848
The only thing left is to rot away.

286
00:21:47,849 --> 00:21:48,766
Don't you think?

287
00:21:50,143 --> 00:21:51,436
Enjoy the movie.

288
00:22:10,788 --> 00:22:12,790
Damn it, why are you following me?

289
00:22:13,833 --> 00:22:14,834
Because I'm worried.

290
00:22:18,463 --> 00:22:20,506
That's a lie.

291
00:22:21,132 --> 00:22:22,050
Because I'm curious?

292
00:22:22,175 --> 00:22:23,176
You psycho…

293
00:22:28,890 --> 00:22:30,141
So that's the face.

294
00:22:31,642 --> 00:22:32,602
What face?

295
00:22:32,727 --> 00:22:35,897
Don't clench your jaw so much. It shows.

296
00:22:36,606 --> 00:22:39,150
That you're embarrassed
but are holding it in.

297
00:22:42,278 --> 00:22:44,739
You're in no position to do this to me.

298
00:22:44,864 --> 00:22:47,158
You can't release that photo anyway.

299
00:22:51,579 --> 00:22:52,455
Director Lee.

300
00:22:53,331 --> 00:22:56,209
You think a single photo
gives you leverage?

301
00:22:57,126 --> 00:23:00,797
That only works
when you can handle the fallout.

302
00:23:00,922 --> 00:23:04,675
Are you sure you can leak that photo

303
00:23:05,843 --> 00:23:07,136
and survive the fallout?

304
00:23:07,261 --> 00:23:08,971
You never know.

305
00:23:10,306 --> 00:23:13,059
As you can see, I'm out of my mind.

306
00:23:13,893 --> 00:23:16,312
So there's no need to provoke me.

307
00:23:17,480 --> 00:23:19,315
What if I actually cause trouble?

308
00:23:19,440 --> 00:23:21,234
Then go ahead.

309
00:23:22,652 --> 00:23:25,571
What? Can't do it
now that you're actually told to?

310
00:24:14,370 --> 00:24:15,371
SIM HAE-JU

311
00:24:18,124 --> 00:24:21,502
Hello, I'm Sim Hae-ju,
the errand boy who does whatever it takes.

312
00:24:21,627 --> 00:24:22,879
Any updates on Director Lee?

313
00:24:23,004 --> 00:24:25,131
The cloud server is tougher to crack.

314
00:24:25,256 --> 00:24:27,842
It has two-factor authentication
and endpoint encryption.

315
00:24:27,967 --> 00:24:30,928
I just tried a brute-force attack
and got kicked out immediately.

316
00:24:31,053 --> 00:24:31,888
It failed.

317
00:24:32,013 --> 00:24:33,139
So?

318
00:24:33,264 --> 00:24:35,141
It'll take at least a day.

319
00:24:35,266 --> 00:24:37,894
Two days if you want no logs left behind.

320
00:24:38,019 --> 00:24:41,105
If it's saved on another cloud,
this is all pointless though.

321
00:24:41,230 --> 00:24:42,982
Just meet with her and negotiate.

322
00:24:43,107 --> 00:24:44,358
That might be faster.

323
00:24:45,026 --> 00:24:47,528
You think I don't know that?

324
00:24:47,653 --> 00:24:49,739
She won't listen to reason.

325
00:24:49,864 --> 00:24:51,741
She's completely crazy.

326
00:24:51,866 --> 00:24:53,743
-Crazier than you?
-Hey.

327
00:24:54,368 --> 00:24:56,787
I'm very reasonable.
Who are you comparing me to?

328
00:24:57,580 --> 00:24:58,581
Whatever.

329
00:24:59,415 --> 00:25:02,460
Blow up the server or nuke the account,
just fix it quickly.

330
00:25:02,585 --> 00:25:04,462
Or I'll blow you up first.

331
00:25:04,587 --> 00:25:06,505
Hey! I thought you were reasonable!

332
00:25:09,008 --> 00:25:10,092
Damn it.

333
00:25:39,413 --> 00:25:40,373
Sir.

334
00:25:47,171 --> 00:25:48,172
Se-ho.

335
00:25:49,090 --> 00:25:50,299
He's already dead.

336
00:25:54,387 --> 00:25:55,471
It wasn't you, right?

337
00:25:56,847 --> 00:25:59,976
You didn't do this, did you?

338
00:26:07,650 --> 00:26:08,609
It was an accident.

339
00:26:09,902 --> 00:26:11,279
Get out of here for now.

340
00:26:11,988 --> 00:26:13,114
Tomorrow's the competition.

341
00:26:13,990 --> 00:26:14,907
Sir!

342
00:26:21,414 --> 00:26:22,331
Ko Yu-seong.

343
00:26:26,127 --> 00:26:28,087
Listen carefully to what I'm about to say.

344
00:26:40,599 --> 00:26:42,518
Hey, say it.

345
00:26:44,228 --> 00:26:47,481
CHAN-HUI

346
00:26:52,862 --> 00:26:54,071
You do page 30.

347
00:26:54,864 --> 00:26:56,824
See this? You do page 20 here.

348
00:26:56,949 --> 00:26:59,702
But this topic here
is closer to what I studied

349
00:26:59,827 --> 00:27:02,371
than the topic on page 20.

350
00:27:02,496 --> 00:27:03,456
Then let's just…

351
00:27:03,581 --> 00:27:06,334
The spark hasn't disappeared
only from my love life.

352
00:27:07,501 --> 00:27:09,003
It suddenly hit me.

353
00:27:10,129 --> 00:27:13,799
When was the last time
my heart raced for something?

354
00:27:14,508 --> 00:27:16,344
When did I last feel a spark?

355
00:27:30,900 --> 00:27:32,610
CHAN-HUI

356
00:28:59,071 --> 00:29:00,281
Stop staring.

357
00:29:01,240 --> 00:29:02,867
This is awkward for me too.

358
00:29:05,035 --> 00:29:06,328
Forget something?

359
00:29:06,454 --> 00:29:07,329
Huh?

360
00:29:09,123 --> 00:29:10,374
Forget what?

361
00:29:17,548 --> 00:29:20,050
-Take it with the Bling Bling app.
-Bling Bling?

362
00:29:24,180 --> 00:29:26,182
Wait, you look so pretty.

363
00:29:29,935 --> 00:29:32,438
Look left. Yes. Make it sexy.

364
00:29:45,326 --> 00:29:47,495
It's nice to go on a date like this.

365
00:29:48,037 --> 00:29:49,455
Brings back old memories.

366
00:29:51,207 --> 00:29:54,001
We should go on dates like this

367
00:29:54,126 --> 00:29:56,629
at least once a year. What do you think?

368
00:29:56,754 --> 00:29:58,756
It builds romantic tension. It's nice.

369
00:29:59,548 --> 00:30:01,509
-Four times.
-What?

370
00:30:01,634 --> 00:30:02,843
Once is too little.

371
00:30:03,844 --> 00:30:05,513
Four times, once a quarter.

372
00:30:07,973 --> 00:30:09,433
What? You don't want to?

373
00:30:49,223 --> 00:30:50,182
Hey, Mi-do.

374
00:30:52,935 --> 00:30:57,815
Your CT and X-rays came back clear,
so it seems to be indigestion.

375
00:30:58,524 --> 00:31:00,317
How long have you had the hiccups?

376
00:31:00,901 --> 00:31:03,362
It's been about a week.

377
00:31:03,487 --> 00:31:05,030
-Right?
-Yes.

378
00:31:06,073 --> 00:31:08,742
This often happens under stress.

379
00:31:08,867 --> 00:31:11,829
If it doesn't stop by this week,
please come back.

380
00:31:11,954 --> 00:31:13,330
Okay, thank you.

381
00:31:20,796 --> 00:31:21,630
YUSEONG UNIVERSITY HOSPITAL

382
00:31:21,755 --> 00:31:23,215
Shouldn't you get a checkup?

383
00:31:24,091 --> 00:31:26,218
-Your last one was last year?
-You're overreacting.

384
00:31:26,343 --> 00:31:27,678
Didn't you hear the doctor--

385
00:31:30,264 --> 00:31:31,223
Book it.

386
00:31:31,932 --> 00:31:33,100
No, I'll do it.

387
00:31:33,225 --> 00:31:36,520
Wait. Then how about this hospital?

388
00:31:39,565 --> 00:31:42,026
-Hey.
-What? Is it bad?

389
00:31:42,610 --> 00:31:45,404
Is that important right now?
What is wrong with you…

390
00:31:48,449 --> 00:31:51,910
What? Why? What? Say it.

391
00:31:53,495 --> 00:31:55,998
Stop. I don't want to fight.

392
00:31:57,916 --> 00:31:58,751
Jeez.

393
00:32:16,143 --> 00:32:18,520
Did you have to bring that up
at the ER, sweetie?

394
00:32:19,438 --> 00:32:22,399
But the hospital said
it wasn't a big deal, sweetie.

395
00:32:22,524 --> 00:32:24,902
And I think this is
more important for us, sweetie.

396
00:32:25,027 --> 00:32:27,321
I just wish we could do it
organically, sweetie.

397
00:32:27,446 --> 00:32:30,783
We agreed to make an effort.
You promised, sweetie.

398
00:32:32,951 --> 00:32:34,119
Okay, sweetie.

399
00:32:34,703 --> 00:32:36,872
But you have to get
a health checkup, sweetie.

400
00:32:36,997 --> 00:32:38,332
Okay, I will, sweetie.

401
00:32:43,754 --> 00:32:44,838
Jeez…

402
00:32:48,092 --> 00:32:49,968
Do we really have to keep doing this?

403
00:32:50,094 --> 00:32:51,178
It worked, didn't it?

404
00:32:51,303 --> 00:32:53,764
Adding "sweetie"
to the end of every sentence

405
00:32:53,889 --> 00:32:57,017
forces us to act cute,
so it softens intense emotions.

406
00:32:59,812 --> 00:33:00,854
Anyway, you promised.

407
00:33:01,689 --> 00:33:03,774
-I'm booking your health checkup.
-Okay, fine.

408
00:33:06,318 --> 00:33:07,444
Oh, right.

409
00:33:07,569 --> 00:33:09,530
Ms. Ma called earlier.

410
00:33:09,655 --> 00:33:13,242
She's clearing out the rooftop studio
and said we can take whatever we want.

411
00:33:13,367 --> 00:33:14,493
When should we go?

412
00:33:14,618 --> 00:33:16,328
She's clearing it out? Why?

413
00:33:17,746 --> 00:33:19,873
QUEENS HAIR SALON

414
00:33:22,668 --> 00:33:24,503
Hey, Namgung.

415
00:33:24,628 --> 00:33:25,963
I just got here.

416
00:33:26,922 --> 00:33:29,925
I'll start clearing it out.
There shouldn't be much.

417
00:33:30,050 --> 00:33:31,135
Yes.

418
00:33:31,260 --> 00:33:32,928
Call me when you get off work.

419
00:33:33,053 --> 00:33:33,887
Okay.

420
00:33:56,201 --> 00:33:57,035
Wow.

421
00:33:58,746 --> 00:34:00,789
It's been a really long time.

422
00:34:02,541 --> 00:34:06,253
I feel like we need a big bang
the moment they walk in.

423
00:34:06,378 --> 00:34:09,214
But they say
that just means a longer shoot

424
00:34:09,339 --> 00:34:10,549
and more prep.

425
00:34:10,674 --> 00:34:12,050
But shouldn't you include it?

426
00:34:12,176 --> 00:34:14,344
Right? I think so too.

427
00:34:14,470 --> 00:34:16,472
-Mi-do, taste this.
-Okay, let me.

428
00:34:18,599 --> 00:34:19,933
-How is it?
-Really good.

429
00:34:20,058 --> 00:34:20,976
-Good?
-Yes.

430
00:34:24,188 --> 00:34:25,022
I'm late.

431
00:34:25,147 --> 00:34:26,273
-I'm off!
-Bye.

432
00:34:29,067 --> 00:34:30,068
-Hey, Mi-do.
-Yes?

433
00:34:30,194 --> 00:34:31,612
Have a bite before you go.

434
00:34:32,321 --> 00:34:33,280
Good luck today.

435
00:34:34,031 --> 00:34:34,907
Okay.

436
00:34:40,788 --> 00:34:42,372
-I'm off.
-See you later.

437
00:34:45,459 --> 00:34:47,795
What kind of directing…

438
00:34:49,129 --> 00:34:50,798
Never mind.

439
00:34:50,923 --> 00:34:52,674
Why do I keep…

440
00:34:57,054 --> 00:34:59,598
No, I'm busy right now.

441
00:35:04,436 --> 00:35:06,438
Hey! Hey, wait a second.

442
00:35:06,563 --> 00:35:08,941
I said no. Wait.

443
00:35:39,471 --> 00:35:40,597
Damn it.

444
00:35:52,985 --> 00:35:53,861
Mr. Namgung.

445
00:35:53,986 --> 00:35:56,071
This is clear WH.

446
00:35:57,239 --> 00:35:58,156
WH?

447
00:35:59,741 --> 00:36:01,994
Oh, workplace harassment?

448
00:36:04,037 --> 00:36:06,999
Two days ago, I analyzed
three years of internal survey data.

449
00:36:07,124 --> 00:36:09,835
Yesterday, I checked all the ingredients
from our peperoncino suppliers.

450
00:36:09,960 --> 00:36:12,754
And today, overtime for farm shipments.

451
00:36:14,089 --> 00:36:15,382
What's this if not WH?

452
00:36:15,507 --> 00:36:18,552
Wow, Ms. Park. You catch on fast.

453
00:36:20,721 --> 00:36:22,598
Are you admitting to workplace harassment?

454
00:36:22,723 --> 00:36:24,933
I don't want to do this either.

455
00:36:26,643 --> 00:36:28,228
But if I don't,

456
00:36:28,353 --> 00:36:30,480
Ms. Park, you'll keep…

457
00:36:31,899 --> 00:36:33,692
focusing on the wrong things.

458
00:36:36,445 --> 00:36:40,574
Two days ago, you were snooping around
raw material specs and guidelines.

459
00:36:42,367 --> 00:36:44,494
Yesterday, you checked partner changes

460
00:36:44,620 --> 00:36:46,079
and unit price adjustments.

461
00:36:47,831 --> 00:36:52,377
Today, you're checking if box lot numbers
and shipping labels can be tampered with,

462
00:36:53,086 --> 00:36:56,048
and if so, who the person
helping from the inside could be.

463
00:36:56,673 --> 00:36:58,258
Weren't you looking for that?

464
00:37:01,678 --> 00:37:03,347
I don't want to do WH, either.

465
00:37:03,472 --> 00:37:04,890
But I've got no choice.

466
00:37:05,015 --> 00:37:07,976
When someone keeps trying
to be a hero at work,

467
00:37:08,101 --> 00:37:09,937
I have to stop them.

468
00:37:13,649 --> 00:37:15,734
I'm not asking for your help.

469
00:37:15,859 --> 00:37:17,945
I won't cause trouble for the team.

470
00:37:19,655 --> 00:37:20,739
Just…

471
00:37:22,074 --> 00:37:24,785
let me handle
the sample processing schedule.

472
00:37:26,370 --> 00:37:27,496
That's not it.

473
00:37:29,373 --> 00:37:30,540
You keep…

474
00:37:32,042 --> 00:37:33,961
making me feel conflicted.

475
00:37:36,964 --> 00:37:38,131
-Should I…
-You startled me!

476
00:37:40,008 --> 00:37:41,927
…tell Executive Director Yoon Do-hak?

477
00:37:42,886 --> 00:37:45,055
Ride his coattails and get promoted?

478
00:37:45,180 --> 00:37:46,431
Aim for director?

479
00:37:48,976 --> 00:37:51,645
What? Did you think
I didn't have that kind of ambition?

480
00:37:52,729 --> 00:37:55,065
So please be careful,

481
00:37:55,190 --> 00:37:57,401
so my ambition
doesn't win over my conscience.

482
00:37:58,568 --> 00:38:00,278
Don't let it hinder work.

483
00:38:00,404 --> 00:38:01,488
Got it?

484
00:38:04,324 --> 00:38:05,867
Where are you going?

485
00:38:06,743 --> 00:38:07,744
To slack off.

486
00:38:17,879 --> 00:38:19,589
SWEET POTATO

487
00:38:25,345 --> 00:38:26,555
Oh my.

488
00:38:26,680 --> 00:38:28,557
Good grief.

489
00:38:28,682 --> 00:38:32,352
Did you do all this by yourself?

490
00:38:33,186 --> 00:38:35,230
Yes. Where is Mr. Namgung?

491
00:38:35,355 --> 00:38:36,398
Assistant Manager Gung?

492
00:38:37,149 --> 00:38:40,068
He's probably at the senior center
with my husband.

493
00:38:41,278 --> 00:38:42,195
Playing…

494
00:38:43,238 --> 00:38:45,699
a solid game of cards.

495
00:38:46,908 --> 00:38:49,411
Jeez, we're shorthanded as it is,

496
00:38:49,536 --> 00:38:51,705
but he's too busy playing around.

497
00:38:52,456 --> 00:38:53,999
Anyway, thank you so much.

498
00:38:54,124 --> 00:38:56,793
You're pretty and a good worker.

499
00:38:58,170 --> 00:39:00,088
You really did a neat, thorough job.

500
00:39:07,471 --> 00:39:11,475
Let's see,  Slam Dunk…

501
00:39:13,351 --> 00:39:14,603
Where is it…

502
00:39:15,562 --> 00:39:17,355
It's not here either.

503
00:39:20,275 --> 00:39:21,109
Huh?

504
00:39:34,998 --> 00:39:37,417
TIN CAN BASTARD

505
00:39:37,542 --> 00:39:39,419
This little bastard, seriously.

506
00:39:41,963 --> 00:39:43,840
Whoa!

507
00:40:26,049 --> 00:40:26,883
Hello?

508
00:40:28,635 --> 00:40:29,469
Director Lee?

509
00:40:29,594 --> 00:40:30,428
TIN CAN BASTARD

510
00:40:32,347 --> 00:40:33,306
Director Lee?

511
00:40:40,897 --> 00:40:42,023
HOW TO STOP HICCUPS

512
00:40:42,190 --> 00:40:45,026
HICCUPS FOR OVER 3 DAYS.
SHOULD I SEE A DOCTOR?

513
00:41:16,933 --> 00:41:17,851
Oh my gosh.

514
00:41:19,060 --> 00:41:20,020
What is it?

515
00:41:20,604 --> 00:41:22,022
I'm thinking…

516
00:41:24,566 --> 00:41:26,443
Right now, on your head,

517
00:41:27,319 --> 00:41:29,654
there's a gigantic spider.

518
00:41:31,573 --> 00:41:32,449
Don't move.

519
00:41:33,825 --> 00:41:35,785
We're in the countryside.
It could be venomous.

520
00:41:35,911 --> 00:41:36,786
What?

521
00:41:39,831 --> 00:41:41,583
During mountain training in the army,

522
00:41:43,001 --> 00:41:45,045
my subordinate got bitten
by a venomous spider.

523
00:41:45,921 --> 00:41:47,214
Did he die?

524
00:41:48,632 --> 00:41:50,383
He didn't die, but…

525
00:41:51,301 --> 00:41:53,261
Oh, do you have a tissue?

526
00:41:53,386 --> 00:41:54,554
I'll get it off.

527
00:42:01,770 --> 00:42:04,481
Are you crazy? What if it's venomous?

528
00:42:15,200 --> 00:42:17,869
It's not funny at all.
Don't ever prank me again.

529
00:42:20,956 --> 00:42:22,916
What are you doing? Throw it away!

530
00:42:24,042 --> 00:42:25,585
You're so cruel.

531
00:42:27,170 --> 00:42:28,838
Spiders are beneficial bugs.

532
00:42:36,012 --> 00:42:37,514
It stubbornly survived

533
00:42:37,639 --> 00:42:40,141
until November.

534
00:42:40,267 --> 00:42:41,726
How could you just kill…

535
00:42:43,937 --> 00:42:45,397
such a strong little guy?

536
00:42:54,572 --> 00:43:01,413
QUEENS HAIR SALON

537
00:43:35,113 --> 00:43:36,156
Director Lee.

538
00:43:37,407 --> 00:43:38,825
Must be glad to see me.

539
00:43:38,950 --> 00:43:41,369
Skip the greetings
and get this off me first.

540
00:43:46,499 --> 00:43:47,334
But wait.

541
00:43:49,044 --> 00:43:51,004
If I help you with this,

542
00:43:51,713 --> 00:43:53,298
will you sign the settlement?

543
00:43:57,886 --> 00:44:00,597
And tell me the login for the photo cloud?

544
00:44:00,722 --> 00:44:01,765
What?

545
00:44:01,890 --> 00:44:02,807
Actually, no.

546
00:44:04,017 --> 00:44:05,935
Maybe it's better if you die like this.

547
00:44:10,315 --> 00:44:12,567
You heard that? I was talking to myself.

548
00:44:12,692 --> 00:44:14,736
The store nearby has a security camera.

549
00:44:15,570 --> 00:44:17,697
It definitely caught you coming in.

550
00:44:17,822 --> 00:44:19,616
And you were my last call.

551
00:44:22,702 --> 00:44:23,953
Well…

552
00:44:25,038 --> 00:44:25,914
So what?

553
00:44:27,874 --> 00:44:30,377
I'll just say you were dead
when I arrived.

554
00:44:31,753 --> 00:44:33,797
You tin can bastard.

555
00:44:35,090 --> 00:44:38,301
A piece of trash
that'll take at least 200 years to rot.

556
00:44:39,344 --> 00:44:41,471
I don't really want to live that long.

557
00:44:42,722 --> 00:44:43,848
Anyway.

558
00:44:46,059 --> 00:44:47,560
Let's see.

559
00:44:48,144 --> 00:44:52,232
This looks like it'll fall
in about ten minutes.

560
00:44:53,608 --> 00:44:55,110
So, care to decide quickly?

561
00:44:57,987 --> 00:44:59,155
Just get lost.

562
00:45:03,827 --> 00:45:04,911
You won't regret it?

563
00:45:12,460 --> 00:45:13,837
Understood.

564
00:45:16,923 --> 00:45:18,591
Crazy bastard.

565
00:45:30,937 --> 00:45:33,440
Good work today.

566
00:45:33,565 --> 00:45:34,732
Here!

567
00:45:35,859 --> 00:45:37,360
Take this home and enjoy.

568
00:45:38,278 --> 00:45:39,237
Thank you.

569
00:45:45,827 --> 00:45:47,537
-Where's Assistant Manager Gung?
-Pardon?

570
00:45:48,371 --> 00:45:51,583
He said he had to check
on the sorting station.

571
00:45:51,708 --> 00:45:53,501
Did he give you a cut?

572
00:45:53,626 --> 00:45:56,546
He completely cleaned up today.

573
00:45:56,671 --> 00:45:59,048
He must've really gone
to the senior center.

574
00:45:59,174 --> 00:46:01,968
Gosh, what made you skip
Hong's Coffee Shop today?

575
00:46:02,093 --> 00:46:05,221
Hey, why bring up
Hong's Coffee Shop right now?

576
00:46:05,346 --> 00:46:07,474
-Come on.
-Then how do you explain the GPS history?

577
00:46:07,599 --> 00:46:09,726
Hong's Coffee Shop
is all over your recent history.

578
00:46:09,851 --> 00:46:10,852
Hong, Hong, Hong!

579
00:46:10,977 --> 00:46:12,395
The GPS route.

580
00:46:16,316 --> 00:46:17,859
Never mind. Keep fighting.

581
00:46:17,984 --> 00:46:19,569
-Huh?
-What?

582
00:46:19,694 --> 00:46:21,321
She said to keep fighting.

583
00:46:21,946 --> 00:46:24,115
If I check the transport driver's GPS,

584
00:46:24,240 --> 00:46:27,494
I might be able to find out
where the switch happens.

585
00:46:29,621 --> 00:46:31,789
Hey, Mr. Oh, you're here.

586
00:46:32,415 --> 00:46:33,750
You left it running, right?

587
00:46:33,875 --> 00:46:35,335
We'll load the goods ourselves,

588
00:46:35,460 --> 00:46:37,545
so go eat and get some rest.

589
00:46:37,670 --> 00:46:38,922
You look exhausted.

590
00:46:39,047 --> 00:46:40,131
Yes, I will.

591
00:46:40,256 --> 00:46:41,382
Thank you.

592
00:46:51,184 --> 00:46:52,852
YANGJIN SWEET POTATO SORTING FACILITY

593
00:47:20,547 --> 00:47:22,131
RECENT ROUTES

594
00:48:03,089 --> 00:48:05,049
I bet people call you stubborn a lot.

595
00:48:06,426 --> 00:48:07,468
No, wait.

596
00:48:07,594 --> 00:48:09,721
Or maybe "nutjob" is more like it?

597
00:48:13,600 --> 00:48:15,768
Just sign the settlement.

598
00:48:16,561 --> 00:48:18,104
It's better than dying.

599
00:48:23,109 --> 00:48:24,611
If you die like this,

600
00:48:24,736 --> 00:48:26,029
what about your family?

601
00:48:27,405 --> 00:48:28,823
Right, what about your boyfriend?

602
00:48:28,948 --> 00:48:30,992
The guy you just got back together with.

603
00:48:31,868 --> 00:48:33,369
I heard you're planning a wedding.

604
00:48:43,254 --> 00:48:44,088
Are you crying?

605
00:48:50,845 --> 00:48:52,305
I've felt this for a while.

606
00:48:53,014 --> 00:48:54,474
You must  really  love him.

607
00:48:55,183 --> 00:48:58,519
It's probably better for Namgung
if I die first.

608
00:48:59,228 --> 00:49:02,231
He gave up everything for my sake.

609
00:49:08,863 --> 00:49:10,823
That just makes me more curious.

610
00:49:13,409 --> 00:49:15,036
I'm asking you one last time.

611
00:49:16,746 --> 00:49:18,706
Are you not going to sign?

612
00:49:22,418 --> 00:49:23,336
Damn it.

613
00:49:40,144 --> 00:49:41,229
You win.

614
00:50:08,172 --> 00:50:09,966
You're bleeding!

615
00:50:27,483 --> 00:50:28,693
Aren't you going to eat?

616
00:50:29,527 --> 00:50:31,779
Traffic will be bad later, so eat up.

617
00:50:35,032 --> 00:50:36,951
Why were you there earlier?

618
00:50:37,076 --> 00:50:38,077
Answer me.

619
00:50:39,203 --> 00:50:40,955
What are you talking about?

620
00:50:41,873 --> 00:50:43,541
Did you have a weird dream?

621
00:50:46,711 --> 00:50:48,671
You pretended you didn't care
in front of me,

622
00:50:48,796 --> 00:50:50,923
but you were secretly investigating
behind my back.

623
00:50:51,048 --> 00:50:53,468
-I never did any such thing.
-Oh.

624
00:50:54,260 --> 00:50:56,387
I guess you're still deciding.

625
00:50:59,140 --> 00:51:00,349
I was wrong about you.

626
00:51:01,350 --> 00:51:04,353
If I had known you were so cowardly
and played it so safe,

627
00:51:04,479 --> 00:51:06,272
I never would've asked you.

628
00:51:06,397 --> 00:51:07,231
My apologies.

629
00:51:14,030 --> 00:51:15,865
I'll handle this alone from now on.

630
00:51:15,990 --> 00:51:17,408
You should stay out of this.

631
00:51:20,369 --> 00:51:22,246
You won't give me that photo, right?

632
00:51:25,708 --> 00:51:26,667
Fine.

633
00:51:27,543 --> 00:51:30,087
I'll just go back and take my own photos.

634
00:51:30,880 --> 00:51:32,840
Sorry for giving you so much trouble.

635
00:51:34,884 --> 00:51:35,927
Sit.

636
00:51:42,433 --> 00:51:44,727
I gave you an inch, and you took a mile.

637
00:51:46,729 --> 00:51:47,647
Cowardly?

638
00:51:49,607 --> 00:51:52,151
This is unbelievable.

639
00:51:53,277 --> 00:51:54,320
Hey.

640
00:51:55,947 --> 00:51:57,240
Hey, Deok-sun.

641
00:51:57,949 --> 00:51:59,367
Look at you now.

642
00:52:04,747 --> 00:52:06,499
You can't get a shot?

643
00:52:06,624 --> 00:52:07,583
SANGJIN UNIVERSITY HOSPITAL

644
00:52:07,708 --> 00:52:09,502
I have an underlying condition.

645
00:52:09,627 --> 00:52:10,795
A condition?

646
00:52:10,920 --> 00:52:11,879
Yes.

647
00:52:12,004 --> 00:52:13,130
Needle phobia.

648
00:52:14,215 --> 00:52:16,843
They said you only need five stitches.

649
00:52:16,968 --> 00:52:19,053
It only hurts when they numb it.

650
00:52:19,178 --> 00:52:21,055
I hate even that brief moment.

651
00:52:22,390 --> 00:52:23,850
It's awful.

652
00:52:26,143 --> 00:52:28,437
You can just disinfect it and bandage it.

653
00:52:28,563 --> 00:52:30,606
And could you prescribe
a week of antibiotics?

654
00:52:31,482 --> 00:52:34,110
But if this goes wrong,

655
00:52:34,235 --> 00:52:36,445
it could lead to necrosis or sepsis.

656
00:52:36,571 --> 00:52:39,282
You really should get stitches.

657
00:52:41,742 --> 00:52:43,494
This one was worse,

658
00:52:43,619 --> 00:52:46,455
but it got better
with just disinfectant and pills.

659
00:52:47,540 --> 00:52:48,666
Could you just do that?

660
00:53:11,105 --> 00:53:13,149
You think this will make me settle?

661
00:53:15,818 --> 00:53:17,069
I doubt you will.

662
00:53:18,362 --> 00:53:20,573
You wouldn't do it to save your own life.

663
00:53:21,824 --> 00:53:23,784
Then why refuse treatment?

664
00:53:23,910 --> 00:53:25,328
I told you.

665
00:53:25,453 --> 00:53:26,954
I have trauma with needles.

666
00:53:27,538 --> 00:53:28,748
You expect me…

667
00:53:30,207 --> 00:53:31,792
to believe that?

668
00:53:35,963 --> 00:53:38,007
Have you ever been poked
under the fingernail?

669
00:53:39,050 --> 00:53:40,343
What are you talking about?

670
00:53:41,260 --> 00:53:42,428
It hurts like hell.

671
00:53:43,679 --> 00:53:47,099
That's how the orphanage director
used to punish us.

672
00:53:47,642 --> 00:53:49,435
To avoid getting caught
during inspections,

673
00:53:49,560 --> 00:53:51,479
they used a method that left no trace.

674
00:53:52,146 --> 00:53:53,940
But more than the pain,

675
00:53:54,065 --> 00:53:55,316
waiting for my turn

676
00:53:56,817 --> 00:53:58,903
was even more terrifying.

677
00:54:04,241 --> 00:54:06,369
Don't look at me like that.

678
00:54:06,494 --> 00:54:08,788
I turned out pretty well for an orphan.

679
00:54:09,789 --> 00:54:10,790
As you can see,

680
00:54:11,749 --> 00:54:12,875
like this.

681
00:54:17,463 --> 00:54:18,589
You're lying, right?

682
00:54:23,052 --> 00:54:24,011
You didn't buy it.

683
00:54:25,388 --> 00:54:26,305
Hey!

684
00:54:26,931 --> 00:54:27,974
Seriously.

685
00:54:29,976 --> 00:54:31,143
Hey.

686
00:54:31,268 --> 00:54:33,521
Where are you?
What happened to the rooftop studio?

687
00:54:33,646 --> 00:54:35,106
Did you do this? Are you hurt?

688
00:54:35,231 --> 00:54:36,524
No, I'm not hurt.

689
00:54:37,191 --> 00:54:38,359
The bookshelf fell over.

690
00:54:41,445 --> 00:54:43,656
Namgung, I'll call you back.

691
00:54:43,781 --> 00:54:44,615
Hello--

692
00:54:50,621 --> 00:54:52,289
Bill me for those car repairs

693
00:54:53,290 --> 00:54:55,209
and for the hospital bill.

694
00:54:56,752 --> 00:54:59,588
We can't meet the settlement terms
you proposed.

695
00:54:59,714 --> 00:55:02,425
No studio in their right mind
would accept that.

696
00:55:03,801 --> 00:55:04,802
Instead,

697
00:55:05,928 --> 00:55:08,472
I think I can get you your job back.

698
00:55:12,059 --> 00:55:13,686
The studio is currently eyeing

699
00:55:13,811 --> 00:55:16,272
Director Kim Jung-man
as your replacement.

700
00:55:17,189 --> 00:55:19,567
You know him, right? From college.

701
00:55:21,527 --> 00:55:23,446
I can dig up some dirt on him.

702
00:55:24,864 --> 00:55:26,282
He has a history of gambling.

703
00:55:26,407 --> 00:55:28,743
I know a few entertainment reporters.

704
00:55:28,868 --> 00:55:32,329
If you give the okay,
I'll get to work right away.

705
00:55:33,456 --> 00:55:35,791
No, I refuse.

706
00:55:37,793 --> 00:55:38,627
Director Lee.

707
00:55:41,630 --> 00:55:42,882
Are you hiding something?

708
00:55:43,632 --> 00:55:44,759
What?

709
00:55:45,926 --> 00:55:47,803
I've found it strange for a while.

710
00:55:48,554 --> 00:55:51,599
All you asked for was
double your directing fee.

711
00:55:51,724 --> 00:55:54,268
Normally, wouldn't
the first thing someone asks for

712
00:55:54,393 --> 00:55:55,686
be to return as director?

713
00:55:56,520 --> 00:55:57,772
But you refused.

714
00:55:57,897 --> 00:56:00,608
It's because your methods are so cheap.

715
00:56:01,358 --> 00:56:02,610
It's so lame.

716
00:56:04,695 --> 00:56:05,613
Oh.

717
00:56:06,947 --> 00:56:08,115
So lame?

718
00:56:09,575 --> 00:56:10,785
Director Lee.

719
00:56:11,535 --> 00:56:12,703
Can I say something crazy?

720
00:56:12,828 --> 00:56:14,455
No, don't.

721
00:56:15,331 --> 00:56:17,166
Keep holding out and you'll break.

722
00:56:18,626 --> 00:56:20,169
Why hold out like this?

723
00:56:21,587 --> 00:56:24,048
With the settlement,
and at the rooftop studio earlier.

724
00:56:24,173 --> 00:56:26,050
Is compromising for once

725
00:56:26,759 --> 00:56:27,968
really that hard?

726
00:56:29,136 --> 00:56:30,638
You were ready to die.

727
00:56:33,933 --> 00:56:35,810
I looked into your background.

728
00:56:38,479 --> 00:56:40,064
It never ends well for you.

729
00:56:42,566 --> 00:56:44,693
What good is all that talent?

730
00:56:45,653 --> 00:56:48,155
You have to know when to compromise.

731
00:56:48,280 --> 00:56:49,615
That's how you survive.

732
00:56:50,908 --> 00:56:51,826
Oh.

733
00:56:53,285 --> 00:56:54,161
Like you?

734
00:56:56,330 --> 00:56:57,998
I looked into you too.

735
00:56:58,124 --> 00:57:01,127
You stick by Seo Ju-hyeok,
being entirely at his beck and call.

736
00:57:01,252 --> 00:57:02,753
You're quite famous for it.

737
00:57:04,380 --> 00:57:06,590
From finding clients to prepping trials.

738
00:57:06,715 --> 00:57:08,092
If that wasn't enough,

739
00:57:08,759 --> 00:57:10,219
you manage his personal life.

740
00:57:11,846 --> 00:57:14,181
Apparently, you do everything
Ju-hyeok tells you to.

741
00:57:15,224 --> 00:57:16,142
Is that so bad?

742
00:57:17,560 --> 00:57:21,021
I just sold my skills
to the person who values them the most.

743
00:57:21,856 --> 00:57:24,316
And I work myself sick to earn that price.

744
00:57:25,442 --> 00:57:27,695
But the way you work is so pathetic.

745
00:57:28,612 --> 00:57:29,613
Have you no shame?

746
00:57:29,738 --> 00:57:32,074
How can anyone walk only on paved roads?

747
00:57:33,159 --> 00:57:36,537
In life, you walk on rough roads
and step in a little mud.

748
00:57:36,662 --> 00:57:39,206
But CEO Seo Ju-hyeok
only walks on paved roads.

749
00:57:39,331 --> 00:57:40,291
Thanks to you.

750
00:57:47,548 --> 00:57:49,258
Can I say something crazy too?

751
00:57:51,468 --> 00:57:53,429
Don't work for the highest bidder.

752
00:57:54,013 --> 00:57:56,307
Work for someone
who treats you like a human.

753
00:57:57,641 --> 00:58:00,644
Because no one considers a dog
their colleague.

754
00:58:06,066 --> 00:58:07,067
So I'm a dog?

755
00:58:07,193 --> 00:58:08,777
A lapdog, to be exact.

756
00:58:09,904 --> 00:58:13,032
A lapdog who could get dumped
by his master any second.

757
00:58:31,800 --> 00:58:32,968
You're pretty funny.

758
00:58:41,852 --> 00:58:43,938
Go ahead and keep acting up.

759
00:58:57,409 --> 00:58:59,495
Go ahead and keep acting up.

760
00:59:05,376 --> 00:59:06,377
I'm joking.

761
00:59:08,963 --> 00:59:10,422
Did I scare you?

762
00:59:14,885 --> 00:59:17,179
Seriously consider returning to directing.

763
00:59:17,888 --> 00:59:22,393
If you want it,
I'll do whatever it takes to get you back.

764
00:59:24,061 --> 00:59:25,771
Crazy bastard.

765
00:59:54,466 --> 00:59:56,302
Honestly, Park Deok-sun…

766
00:59:57,845 --> 00:59:59,596
How has she not changed a bit?

767
01:00:07,896 --> 01:00:08,939
Mi-do, you're home?

768
01:00:09,606 --> 01:00:10,524
Yes.

769
01:00:12,526 --> 01:00:14,486
I'm making  tteokbokki.  Hang on.

770
01:00:45,768 --> 01:00:46,894
Mi-do, what's wrong?

771
01:01:11,752 --> 01:01:12,628
Oh?

772
01:01:13,504 --> 01:01:15,214
Your hiccups stopped.

773
01:01:15,923 --> 01:01:17,674
No, they'll come back soon.

774
01:01:22,054 --> 01:01:23,347
No, they stopped.

775
01:01:24,473 --> 01:01:25,307
Oh?

776
01:01:26,392 --> 01:01:28,811
Nothing worked before. How did they stop?

777
01:01:29,478 --> 01:01:30,521
Good question.

778
01:01:31,939 --> 01:01:33,524
They really did stop.

779
01:01:34,733 --> 01:01:35,984
TIN CAN BASTARD

780
01:01:36,693 --> 01:01:37,986
PARK SU-A

781
01:01:45,452 --> 01:01:47,996
TIN CAN BASTARD

782
01:01:51,625 --> 01:01:54,169
PARK SU-A

783
01:02:18,277 --> 01:02:19,319
THANK YOU TO KIM DA-HUIN, PARK SUNG-HOON,
AND NAM DA-REUM

784
01:02:19,445 --> 01:02:20,529
FOR THEIR SPECIAL APPEARANCE

785
01:02:23,240 --> 01:02:24,783
I hope everyone criticizes you.

786
01:02:26,535 --> 01:02:28,120
Were you going to keep pretending
you don't know me?

787
01:02:28,245 --> 01:02:29,621
-Yes.
-"Yes"?

788
01:02:29,746 --> 01:02:30,956
ANY SPARE MONEY?
I NEED TWO MILLION WON MORE THIS MONTH.

789
01:02:31,081 --> 01:02:33,000
-Come back as a director?
-You said you could.

790
01:02:33,125 --> 01:02:35,085
-Of course.
-Yes! Right on!

791
01:02:35,210 --> 01:02:37,045
-I don't think I can do it.
-What?

792
01:02:37,171 --> 01:02:39,006
Life isn't like dramas.

793
01:02:39,131 --> 01:02:42,676
Do what you enjoy
for the rest of your life.

794
01:02:42,801 --> 01:02:43,635
That suits you.

795
01:02:43,760 --> 01:02:46,388
If you mess with him, I'll kill you.

796
01:02:47,181 --> 01:02:48,724
Maybe I should mess with him.

797
01:02:48,849 --> 01:02:50,934
I think it would be fun.

798
01:02:51,643 --> 01:02:53,604
Subtitle translation by Soya Back
